  "Number": 6,
  "Question": "If \\(f(x)=4^x,\\) then \\(f(x+1)-f(x)\\) equals:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(4\\)",
    "B": "\\(f(x)\\)",
    "C": "\\(2f(x)\\)",
    "D": "\\(3f(x)\\)",
    "E": "\\(4f(x)\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Increasing the exponent of \\(4\\) by \\(1\\) multiplies its value by \\(4\\). Thus, for every real \\(x\\),\n\\[\nf(x+1)=4^{x+1}=4\\cdot4^x=4f(x).\n\\]\nSubtracting \\(f(x)\\) gives\n\\[\nf(x+1)-f(x)=4f(x)-f(x)=\\boxed{3f(x)}.\n\\]\nThe answer is choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
